# Clarifying questions (Global)

- Default: proceed with safe, bounded assumptions when missing info won’t cause major rework.
- Ask questions only when it’s high leverage or risky (max 2 questions per turn):
  - destructive/irreversible actions, security/auth, prod-impacting changes, ambiguous target files/modules, competing interpretations.
- When asking, provide 2–3 options + a recommended default.
- If the user doesn’t answer: proceed with the safest default; avoid irreversible actions.
- Only include **Assumptions** when they affect behavior.
